  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced social dialogue National Tripartite Platform</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Seychelles aims to strengthen social dialogue by December 2023 through the renewal and validation of the Industrial Relations Act (IRA) based on the review outcomes.

The objective is to renew and validate the IRA to promote social dialogue, tripartism, and sound labor regulation.

A comprehensive review of the current IRA will be conducted, engaging relevant stakeholders such as government agencies, employers&apos; organizations, and workers&apos; unions. The review will assess the effectiveness of the Act in fostering social dialogue and tripartism, alignment with current labor market trends and best practices, and areas for improvement to promote harmonious labor relations and decent work conditions.

Based on the review findings, recommendations for updating the IRA will be developed, addressing identified gaps and leveraging best practices to enhance mechanisms for facilitating and promoting effective social dialogue, tripartite collaboration, and sound labor regulations.

The renewed Industrial Relations Act will be formally adopted and implemented following thorough consultation with stakeholders and consideration of expert recommendations.

By renewing and validating the Industrial Relations Act, Seychelles aims to strengthen and institutionalize social dialogue as a key mechanism for addressing labor market challenges, foster collaboration, and achieve consensus on workplace issues.

The country also aims to enhance tripartism by actively engaging and empowering representatives from government, employers, and workers in shaping labor policies and promoting decent work practices.

Additionally, Seychelles aims to develop and implement sound labor regulations that strike a balance between safeguarding worker rights and fostering a conducive business environment.

This initiative will contribute to achieving the indicator: &quot;Number of Member States in which there are newly established or strengthened institutions and processes for social dialogue.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
